::ENG3_U03_L03_Q23::[MLA.ENG3.R.07] Passage: If peace is desired, prepare justice before swords. A treaty signed by frightened hands will tear when fear changes direction. What is the author's purpose? {
~A. To argue that fear creates lasting peace.#The passage says fear-based treaties tear. Recheck the passage, context, or task wording and choose the option that preserves meaning and matches the standard.
~B. To give instructions for sword storage.#Swords are part of a political image. Recheck the passage, context, or task wording and choose the option that preserves meaning and matches the standard.
~C. To claim treaties are never useful.#The passage critiques treaties based only on fear. Recheck the passage, context, or task wording and choose the option that preserves meaning and matches the standard.
=D. To persuade leaders that lasting peace depends on justice, not fear.#Correct. The passage contrasts justice with fear. Notice how the answer uses the exact wording, evidence, or concept required by the standard.
}

