~A. "peace is desired"#This states the situation. Recheck the passage, context, or task wording and choose the option that preserves meaning and matches the standard.
~B. "before swords"#This supports the contrast but is less vivid than the tearing treaty. Recheck the passage, context, or task wording and choose the option that preserves meaning and matches the standard.
=C. "will tear when fear changes direction"#Correct. This image shows why fear-based peace is unstable. Notice how the answer uses the exact wording, evidence, or concept required by the standard.
~D. "If peace"#This is an opening condition. Recheck the passage, context, or task wording and choose the option that preserves meaning and matches the standard.
}

